00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,359
Speaker 1: He opened not his mouth.

216
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,040
Speaker 1: It means me too.

217
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,319
Speaker 1: I have no excuse.

218
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,480
Speaker 1: I must learn to close.

219
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:24,560
Speaker 1: What are you going to tell him?

220
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:27,920
Speaker 1: What are they going to tell?

221
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:33,920
Speaker 1: So now we must be imitators of Christ.

222
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,960
Speaker 1: Imitators of Christ.

223
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,160
Speaker 1: He's a good example.

224
00:17:40,570 --> 00:17:42,890
Speaker 1: And these are part of the benefits of the incarnation.

225
00:17:43,050 --> 00:17:45,610
Speaker 1: The Bible says John 1:18.

226
00:17:46,090 --> 00:17:47,850
Speaker 1: No one had seen God at any time.

227
00:17:49,210 --> 00:17:52,850
Speaker 1: The only begotten Son of God who is in the bosom of the Father has declared Him.

228
00:17:52,850 --> 00:18:02,730
Speaker 1: It means, like I shared last week, he came to the earth to show us who God is and what God is.

229
00:18:02,730 --> 00:18:06,730
Speaker 1: Like he showed us firsthand because he is God.

230
00:18:08,970 --> 00:18:12,770
Speaker 1: And in him we see the fullness of the Godhead.

231
00:18:12,770 --> 00:18:15,170
Speaker 1: Bodily we know for a fact.

232
00:18:15,170 --> 00:18:23,130
Speaker 1: In fact, in him we can see some things that were not the full expression of the nature of God in the law.

233
00:18:24,330 --> 00:18:28,730
Speaker 1: We see that God is merciful, slow to anger, plentious in grace.

234
00:18:28,970 --> 00:18:30,410
Speaker 1: Come on, I get what I'm saying.

235
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:33,780
Speaker 1: He declared God to us.

\n